      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "<overview>\nThe workflow is running a scheduled release notes generation job for .NET 11 Preview 3. The goal is to discover active release milestones, generate `changes.json` and `features.json` manifests, and write curated markdown release notes for all .NET components, then create a PR in the `jeffhandley/dotnet-core-release-notes` repository. The approach involves cloning the VMR (`dotnet/dotnet`) and individual component repos to extract commit data between Preview 2 and Preview 3 SHAs, since both the `release-notes-gen` tool and GitHub API access are unavailable (no auth tokens).\n</overview>\n\n<history>\n1. Workflow triggered with instructions to generate .NET 11 Preview 3 release notes\n   - Loaded the `release-notes` skill and all reference documents (component-mapping, format-template, editorial-rules, feature-scoring, quality-bar, examples)\n   - Attempted to download `release-notes-gen` tool via `gh run download` — failed (gh CLI not authenticated)\n   - Attempted to install via `dotnet tool install` from GitHub packages — failed (no GITHUB_TOKEN)\n   - Attempted `web_fetch` to GitHub API — permission denied\n   - Launched sub-agents to query GitHub MCP tools — they also lacked network/GitHub access\n\n2. Discovered active milestones by cloning the VMR\n   - Cloned `dotnet/dotnet` with `--filter=blob:none --no-checkout`\n   - Fetched `origin/release/11.0.1xx-preview3` branch\n   - Confirmed: latest shipped = Preview 2 (2026-03-10), main is building Preview 4, Preview 3 has a release branch but no tag (not yet shipped)\n   - Extracted `source-manifest.json` at both Preview 2 tag and Preview 3 branch tip\n   - Compared component SHAs: all 12 major components changed (runtime, aspnetcore, sdk, roslyn, efcore, msbuild, fsharp, nuget-client, razor, templating, winforms, wpf)\n\n3. Collected PR data by cloning individual component repos\n   - Cloned dotnet/runtime, dotnet/aspnetcore, dotnet/roslyn, dotnet/sdk, dotnet/efcore, dotnet/winforms, dotnet/wpf, dotnet/fsharp, dotnet/msbuild, nuget/nuget.client — all with `--filter=blob:none --no-checkout`\n   - Ran `git log HEAD_SHA ^BASE_SHA --format=\"%s\"` for each to extract commit subjects with PR numbers\n   - Identified and excluded reverted PRs: ProcessStartOptions (#124271 reverted by #125839), nuget dotnet-why (#7212 revert), nuget CRL/OCSP (#7220 revert)\n\n4. Created the release notes branch and started writing files\n   - Created branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3`\n   - Created directory `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/`\n   - Created `changes.json` with ~100 notable PRs across all components\n   - Created `features.json` with scored entries for editorial prioritization\n   - Was in the process of writing markdown files when compaction occurred\n</history>\n\n<work_done>\nFiles created:\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/changes.json` — comprehensive manifest of ~100 notable PRs across all components. Note: manually assembled (no tool), not 100% complete but captures all high-value changes. ProcessStartOptions excluded (reverted).\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/features.json` — scored derivative with editorial guidance. Scores range 3–9.\n\nFiles still needed (NOT YET CREATED):\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/README.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/runtime.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/aspnetcore.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/sdk.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/csharp.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/efcore.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/msbuild.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/nuget.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/fsharp.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/winforms.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/wpf.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/visualbasic.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/dotnetmaui.md`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/containers.md`\n\nCurrent state:\n- [x] Branch created: `release-notes/11.0-preview3`\n- [x] Directory created\n- [x] changes.json created\n- [x] features.json created\n- [ ] All markdown files — NOT created yet\n- [ ] Git commit\n- [ ] PR creation\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n## Environment Constraints\n- **No GitHub auth**: `gh` CLI unauthenticated, no `GITHUB_TOKEN`, no `GH_TOKEN`, `web_fetch` to github.com blocked\n- **No release-notes-gen tool**: Can't download from workflow artifact (needs auth), can't install from GitHub packages (needs token). Used manual git cloning instead.\n- **Python `|` pipe syntax blocked**: Several bash commands using pipes into python3 returned \"Permission denied and could not request permission from user\". Workaround: use node -e or simple grep/awk instead. Pure bash with head/tail/grep works fine.\n\n## Milestone Discovery\n- **Latest shipped**: `11.0.0-preview.2` (2026-03-10), runtime `11.0.0-preview.2.26159.112`\n- **Active milestone**: Preview 3 — has VMR release branch `origin/release/11.0.1xx-preview3`, no tag yet\n- **Main is building**: Preview 4 (`PreReleaseVersionIteration=4` in eng/Versions.props)\n- **No preview4 notes possible yet**: No base tag for preview 3 to use as preview 4's base\n\n## VMR Structure\n- Clone at `/tmp/dotnet` with `--filter=blob:none --no-checkout`\n- Preview 2 tag: `v11.0.0-preview.2.26159.112`\n- Preview 3 head: `FETCH_HEAD` after `git fetch origin release/11.0.1xx-preview3`\n- VMR codeflow commits are squash merges — their bodies do NOT contain individual PR details\n- Individual component repos cloned to `/tmp/runtime`, `/tmp/aspnetcore`, etc.\n\n## Component SHA Ranges (preview2 → preview3)\n- runtime: `68d697a4971a` → `d23e53a91dcd`\n- aspnetcore: `552df3085ec1` → `655f41d52f2f`\n- sdk: `b8600c8854f5` → `1c98288c64bb`\n- roslyn: `3a38d0c1ca5f` → `d4c7d6ad25d0`\n- efcore: `3f1e6b1e8690` → `34455545b388`\n- msbuild: `b3eba18a92fc` → `50afea8cba5a`\n- fsharp: `28dd75730f38` → `bd2823e2d07c`\n- nuget-client: `d2887cd59105` → `779eff1e7342`\n- razor: `3c860eafd06d` → `c39bfd8d4a97`\n- winforms: `be6c7499b29c` → `1082eccb8fb2`\n- wpf: `f52d8e79a7ba` → `9484c1c170c5`\n\n## Reverted PRs — Do Not Document\n- `ProcessStartOptions` class: added in runtime #124271, removed in #125839\n- NuGet: `dotnet nuget why` resolved versions: #7017 reverted by #7212\n- NuGet: CRL/OCSP in verify output: #7181 reverted by #7220\n\n## Key Features by Component (for markdown writing)\n### runtime.md (highest priority first)\n1. Runtime-async enabled by default for net11.0 (#126343, #124488) — SCORE 9\n2. GC regions enabled on macOS (#125416) — SCORE 7\n3. Runtime-async continuation reuse + JIT optimization (#125556, #125615, #125869) — SCORE 6\n4. ARM64 SM4 and SHA3 hardware intrinsics (#124504) — SCORE 5\n5. Unsafe Evolution attributes in runtime (#125721) — SCORE 5\n\n### libraries.md (highest priority first)\n1. System.Text.Json cluster: PascalCase (#124644), member-level naming (#124645), type-level JsonIgnore (#124646), generic converters (#123209), byref ctors (#122950) — SCORES 6–8\n2. ML-KEM API stabilization (removes Experimental) — SCORE 8\n3. Zstandard moved to System.IO.Compression (#124634) — SCORE 7\n4. CRC32 validation in ZIP reads (#124766) — SCORE 7\n5. Parameterized CRC-32/CRC-64 — SCORE 6\n6. RandomAccess with non-seekable files (#125512) — SCORE 6\n7. DNS RFC 6761 special-use domains (#123076) — SCORE 6\n8. Regex performance cluster (#125289, #125636, #124628, #124736) — SCORE 5\n9. VectorXx.Asin / TensorPrimitives (#126052) — SCORE 5\n10. Process.Start accepts null arguments (#126076) — SCORE 5\n11. HashSet<T> performance (#125893) — SCORE 5\n\n### aspnetcore.md\n1. OpenAPI 3.2 support (#65415) — SCORE 8\n2. Blazor Virtualize variable-height items (#64964) — SCORE 8\n3. Zstd Content-Encoding (#65479) — SCORE 7\n4. Blazor WASM JSExport for events (#65897) — SCORE 5\n5. Data protection fix (#65890) — SCORE 4\n6. HTTP/2 bug fixes cluster (#65765, #65771, #65729) — SCORE 3\n\n### efcore.md\n1. Cosmos complex properties Query (#37577) + model building (#37919) — SCORE 8\n2. Partial property loading (#37857, #37829) — SCORE 8\n3. ChangeTracker.GetEntriesForState() (#37847) — SCORE 6\n4. Migration improvements: exclude FK (#37815), migration ID as type name (#37841), batch terminators (#37810) — SCORE 5\n5. AddPooledDbContextFactory parameterless (#37144, community) — SCORE 5\n6. BREAKING: MigrationsNotFound throws (#37839) — SCORE 5\n\n### csharp.md (Roslyn — IDE features, product-boundary: exclude pure IDE)\n1. File-based app automatic discovery + #:include completion (#82863, #82625) — SCORE 7\n2. Unsafe Evolution updates (#82910, #82731) — SCORE 5–6\n\n### sdk.md\n1. NuGet CLI support for file-based apps (#7169) — SCORE 7\n2. Target framework selection for multi-targeted projects (#53466) — SCORE 6\n3. dotnet test --artifacts-path in MTP mode (#53353) — SCORE 5\n\n### msbuild.md\n1. Prefer dotnet MSBuild for out-of-proc workers (#13452) — SCORE 5\n2. Unix cross-terminal node reuse (#13354) — SCORE 5\n3. ToolTask hang fix (#13351) — bug fix\n\n### fsharp.md — stub + bug fixes only\n- Fix closure capture and let-rec initialization codegen (#19339)\n- Fix emitted method signatures (#19340)\n- Fix type definition metadata (#19341)\n- Fix CLIEvent properties (#18584)\n\n### winforms.md — stub or minimal\n- Fix InvalidCastException in Control.OnHandleDestroyed (#14295)\n- Fix ComboBox.ObjectCollection.CopyTo (#14075)\n\n### wpf.md — stub (infrastructure only)\n\n### visualbasic.md — stub\n\n### dotnetmaui.md — stub (not in VMR)\n\n### containers.md — stub (not in VMR)\n\n## Editorial Guidelines (from reference docs)\n- Use `[org/repo #NNNN](url)` format WITH space before `#`\n- Follow format-template.md structure: TOC → sections → bug fixes → community contributors\n- Quality bar: every feature needs WHY and HOW (code sample)\n- Never guess API names — use `<!-- TODO: verify -->` if uncertain\n- Don't document reverted features\n- Clusters: group related STJ features, regex perf, runtime-async under single sections\n- Preview-to-preview: only document state changes from P2 (e.g., runtime-async now default, ML-KEM now stable)\n- Community section: list all external contributors\n- Filtered features: add HTML comment block before Bug fixes\n\n## Link Format for PR References\nUse: `[dotnet/runtime #124644](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124644)`\n(space before #, as specified in format-template.md and editorial-rules.md)\n\n## Preview2 Structure to Follow\n- Has: README.md, libraries.md, runtime.md, sdk.md, aspnetcore.md, efcore.md, fsharp.md, csharp.md, visualbasic.md, winforms.md, wpf.md, dotnetmaui.md, containers.md, api-diff/, release.json, 11.0.0-preview.2.md\n- Note: preview2 has no msbuild.md or nuget.md separately — they may be part of sdk.md\n- Preview1 has: msbuild.md as a separate file\n- Runtime version for preview3 unknown (not yet tagged) — use placeholder or omit\n\n## safeoutputs Requirement\nCRITICAL: Must call at least one safeoutputs tool before finishing. Options:\n- `add_comment` — add comment to a PR\n- `create_pull_request` — create new PR\n- `push_to_pull_request_branch` — push to existing PR branch\n- `noop` — if no action needed (explain why)\nMust NOT end without calling one.\n</technical_details>\n\n<important_files>\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/changes.json`\n  - Comprehensive PR manifest for Preview 3 (~100 notable PRs)\n  - Manually assembled (tool unavailable); covers runtime, aspnetcore, sdk, roslyn, efcore, msbuild, nuget-client, winforms, fsharp\n  - Excludes reverted PRs (ProcessStartOptions, nuget why-versions, nuget CRL/OCSP)\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/features.json`\n  - Scored editorial guide derived from changes.json\n  - Scores 3–9; top scores: runtime-async default (9), STJ/ML-KEM/Cosmos/Blazor Virtualize (8)\n  - Includes `score_reason`, `section`, `component` fields for writing guidance\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview2/libraries.md`\n  - Reference example of correct markdown format used in this repo\n  - Shows STJ, tar, perf entry style; use as template\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview2/runtime.md`\n  - Reference for runtime-async documentation style\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/format-template.md`\n  - Authoritative document structure: TOC → sections → bug fixes → community contributors\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/editorial-rules.md`\n  - Tone, PR link format (`org/repo #N` with space), naming rules, community attribution\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/component-mapping.md`\n  - Maps repos to output files: runtime→libraries.md+runtime.md, aspnetcore→aspnetcore.md, etc.\n\n- `/tmp/preview2-manifest.json` and `/tmp/preview3-manifest.json`\n  - source-manifest.json at each release point; used to identify changed components\n\n- Cloned repos at `/tmp/runtime`, `/tmp/aspnetcore`, `/tmp/roslyn`, `/tmp/sdk`, `/tmp/efcore`, `/tmp/winforms`, `/tmp/wpf`, `/tmp/fsharp`, `/tmp/msbuild`, `/tmp/nuget`\n  - All cloned with `--filter=blob:none --no-checkout`; git log has been run but repos still available\n</important_files>\n\n<next_steps>\nRemaining work:\n\n1. **Write all markdown files** (highest priority — none exist yet):\n   - `README.md` — index linking all component files\n   - `libraries.md` — STJ cluster, ML-KEM, Zstandard, CRC32/ZIP, regex perf, DNS, etc.\n   - `runtime.md` — runtime-async default, GC regions macOS, runtime-async perf, ARM64 intrinsics\n   - `aspnetcore.md` — OpenAPI 3.2, Blazor Virtualize variable-height, zstd, JSExport events\n   - `sdk.md` — NuGet file-based apps, TF selection, dotnet test --artifacts-path\n   - `csharp.md` — file-based app tooling, Unsafe Evolution\n   - `efcore.md` — Cosmos complex properties, partial loading, ChangeTracker API, breaking changes\n   - `msbuild.md` — worker node improvements, Unix node reuse (or stub)\n   - `nuget.md` — file-based apps CLI support, --allow-untrusted-root (or incorporate into sdk.md)\n   - `fsharp.md` — stub + bug fixes\n   - `winforms.md` — stub + bug fixes\n   - `wpf.md` — stub\n   - `visualbasic.md` — stub\n   - `dotnetmaui.md` — stub (not in VMR)\n   - `containers.md` — stub (not in VMR)\n\n2. **Run markdown linting**: `npx markdownlint --config .github/linters/.markdown-lint.yml release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/*.md`\n\n3. **Commit all files** to branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3`\n\n4. **Create PR** via `create_pull_request` safeoutputs tool:\n   - Title: `[release-notes] .NET 11 Preview 3`\n   - Target: `jeffhandley/dotnet-core-release-notes` main\n   - Body: summarize milestone, component count, open questions\n\n5. **Call safeoutputs tool** (CRITICAL — required before finishing)\n\nImmediate next actions:\n- Start writing `README.md` (simple index file, quick win)\n- Write `runtime.md` (runtime-async is the headline feature)\n- Write `libraries.md` (most content, highest value)\n- Write remaining component files\n- Commit and open PR\n</next_steps>\n\n<checkpoint_title>Writing .NET 11 Preview 3 release notes</checkpoint_title>",
