              "name": "create",
              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# .NET SDK in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes the following SDK updates:\\n\\n- [NuGet support for file-based apps](#nuget-support-for-file-based-apps)\\n- [Target framework selection for multi-targeted projects](#target-framework-selection-for-multi-targeted-projects)\\n- [dotnet test --artifacts-path in MTP mode](#dotnet-test---artifacts-path-in-mtp-mode)\\n\\n## NuGet support for file-based apps\\n\\nFile-based app support (`.cs` files with top-level statements and no `.csproj`) now integrates with the NuGet CLI ([nuget/nuget.client #7169](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7169)). You can use `dotnet nuget` commands to add, update, or remove package directives in single-file `.cs` scripts.\\n\\n```bash\\n# Add a NuGet package to a single-file app\\ndotnet nuget add package Newtonsoft.Json --source-file app.cs\\n\\n# Remove a package reference from a single-file app\\ndotnet nuget remove package Newtonsoft.Json --source-file app.cs\\n```\\n\\nThe package directive is stored as a `#:package` comment at the top of the `.cs` file:\\n\\n```csharp\\n#:package Newtonsoft.Json@13.0.3\\n\\nusing Newtonsoft.Json;\\nvar result = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(new { message = \\\"hello\\\" });\\nConsole.WriteLine(result);\\n```\\n\\nThis extends the file-based app experience introduced in earlier previews and paired with C# tooling updates in Preview 3 ([dotnet/roslyn #82863](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82863)).\\n\\n## Target framework selection for multi-targeted projects\\n\\n`dotnet run`, `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, and related commands now accept a `-f` / `--framework` flag when working with multi-targeted projects ([dotnet/sdk #53466](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/53466)). Previously, specifying a single TFM for a multi-targeted build required environment variables or project properties.\\n\\n```bash\\n# Run only the net11.0 target of a multi-targeted library\\ndotnet run -f net11.0\\n\\n# Build only the net8.0 target\\ndotnet build -f net8.0\\n```\\n\\n## dotnet test --artifacts-path in MTP mode\\n\\n`dotnet test` now respects the `--artifacts-path` option when running in Microsoft Testing Platform (MTP) mode ([dotnet/sdk #53353](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/53353)). This allows you to redirect test output, logs, and result files to a consistent directory regardless of whether you're using VSTest or MTP.\\n\\n```bash\\ndotnet test --artifacts-path ./test-results\\n```\\n\\nTest result files, coverage reports, and crash dumps produced during the run are placed in the specified directory.\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed `dotnet publish` producing incorrect intermediate output paths when `PublishDir` contains spaces ([dotnet/sdk #53148](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/53148))\\n- Fixed `dotnet workload update` failing when a workload manifest has been removed from the feed ([dotnet/sdk #53280](https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/pull/53280))\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/sdk.md\"}"
