              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# C# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes updates to C# tooling and the Roslyn compiler:\\n\\n- [File-based app tooling: auto-discovery and #:include completion](#file-based-app-tooling)\\n- [Unsafe Evolution attributes](#unsafe-evolution-attributes)\\n\\nC# updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in C# 14](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/csharp-14)\\n\\n## File-based app tooling\\n\\nC# 14 Preview 3 adds IDE tooling support for the file-based app feature, which allows running `.cs` files directly without a project file.\\n\\n### Automatic file-based app discovery\\n\\nThe language service now automatically detects single-file C# scripts and activates file-based app support without requiring a manual project association ([dotnet/roslyn #82863](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82863)). Opening a `.cs` file with top-level statements in an editor no longer shows \\\"no project\\\" errors; IntelliSense, diagnostics, and navigation work out of the box.\\n\\n### #:include directive completion\\n\\nEditors now provide completion for `#:include` directives in file-based apps ([dotnet/roslyn #82625](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82625)). The `#:include` directive allows splitting a file-based app across multiple `.cs` files, and completion now shows the available files relative to the script's location.\\n\\n```csharp\\n// app.cs\\n#:include helpers.cs\\n#:package Newtonsoft.Json@13.0.3\\n\\nusing Newtonsoft.Json;\\nvar result = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(new { message = \\\"hello\\\" });\\nConsole.WriteLine(result);\\n```\\n\\n## Unsafe Evolution attributes\\n\\n> This is a preview feature for .NET 11.\\n\\nThe Unsafe Evolution API pattern ([dotnet/runtime #125721](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125721)) gets compiler support in Preview 3. The new `[UnsafeEvolutionAttribute]` lets library authors mark APIs where the type layout or ABI may change in future versions, asking callers to acknowledge the risk at the call site.\\n\\nRoslyn surfaced updates for Unsafe Evolution in two PRs:\\n\\n- **Unsafe Evolution in roslyn** ([dotnet/roslyn #82910](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82910)): compiler recognizes the attribute and emits diagnostics when callers omit the required acknowledgment\\n- **UnsafeEvolutionAttribute diagnostics** ([dotnet/roslyn #82731](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82731)): improved diagnostic messages and IDE quick-fixes\\n\\nThis feature is targeted at library authors building low-level, performance-sensitive code that must evolve without breaking binary compatibility. End users of those libraries will see a diagnostic asking them to opt in when consuming an unsafe-evolution API.\\n\\nThis is a preview feature and the design may evolve before the final .NET 11 release.\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/csharp.md\"}"
            }
          }
        ],
