              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# NuGet in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes the following NuGet updates:\\n\\n- [File-based app support in NuGet CLI](#file-based-app-support-in-nuget-cli)\\n- [--allow-untrusted-root for dotnet nuget trust](#--allow-untrusted-root-for-dotnet-nuget-trust)\\n\\nNuGet updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [NuGet release notes](https://learn.microsoft.com/nuget/release-notes/)\\n\\n## File-based app support in NuGet CLI\\n\\nNuGet CLI commands now support file-based apps — single `.cs` files that run without a `.csproj` ([nuget/nuget.client #7169](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7169)). The `dotnet nuget add package` and `dotnet nuget remove package` commands accept a `--source-file` option to specify the `.cs` file, and the package reference is stored as a `#:package` directive at the top of the file.\\n\\nSee [SDK: NuGet support for file-based apps](./sdk.md#nuget-support-for-file-based-apps) for full details.\\n\\n## --allow-untrusted-root for dotnet nuget trust\\n\\n`dotnet nuget trust` now accepts `--allow-untrusted-root` ([nuget/nuget.client #7224](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7224)). This option tells the NuGet trust store to accept certificates whose root CA is not installed in the system trust store. It is intended for enterprise and air-gapped scenarios where packages are signed with internally issued certificates.\\n\\n```bash\\ndotnet nuget trust author \\\"MyCorp\\\" --certificate-fingerprint <sha256> --allow-untrusted-root\\n```\\n\\n## Bug fixes\\n\\n- Fixed package restore failing when a lock file contains a package reference to a floating version that resolves to a pre-release ([nuget/nuget.client #7195](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7195))\\n- Fixed `dotnet nuget push` not retrying on `429 Too Many Requests` responses from package sources ([nuget/nuget.client #7200](https://github.com/nuget/nuget.client/pull/7200))\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-